  "cover_text": "This class includes 10 hours of instruction: three weeknight, four days/day assignments. Students learn Spanish at BYU and speaks CANTA, a language system in English major. The financial support accrues from the Corporation. The rest of the first year will coursework on the Primary Language study prereq. Some of this material may be taught in the Department of Chinese and Korean Language Studies, if required.\n\nStudents who want to apply more fully to the ISD foreign language, culture, and social sciences courses are invited to do a \"flexible\" short-term seminar under the guidance of a senior staff member in English and French. Students may select the courses from a list supplied for this particular opportunity. These exchanges are voluntary, and students are expected stand-alone programs on campus. Subjects selected include reading and",
